<title>USA: Consolidated Papers sees $200 mln spending.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Papers sees $200 mln spending.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Papers Inc expects capital spending of $200 million in 1997 to sustain and improve its operations, the company said in its annual report.</p>
<p>In 1996, its expenditures totaled $288 million and included funding for continuing construction of a new paper machine at the Stevens Point (Wisconsin) Division. That machine is expected to boost capacity of the mill 56 percent.</p>
<p>Consolidated Papers, based in Wisconsin Rapids, Wis., produces coated printing papers and glossy stock for catalogs and magazines.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
